#import "../preamble.typ": *

#set par(first-line-indent: 0em)

Enforcement of privacy and security policies becomes practical in real
applications when policies leverage shared, high-level vocabularies, authored by
experts, that are legible to users and mechanically lower to sound enforcement.

#v(2em)

Vocabularies allow for a division of labor where no single involved party needs
complete expertise. Experts establish the vocabulary once, bootstrapping
soundness. Users build on top of the vocabulary, reusing and recombining it. By
employing experts sparingly and empowering users, the vocabulary allows the
enforcement to scale to real-world scale while at the same time leaving unsound
assistive techniques, such as AI, off the critical path.


